---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { companyInfo } from '../lib/catalog';
---
<BaseLayout title="Terms & Conditions | Tripadi International" description="Terms and conditions for use of the Tripadi International website and for retail orders placed through it.">
  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container-prose">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.025em] text-ink-900 md:text-5xl">Terms & conditions</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[14px] text-ink-500">Applies to this website and to retail orders placed through it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="container-prose prose-editorial mt-10">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {companyInfo.name}, a manufacturer and exporter of metalware, of {companyInfo.address.city},
        {companyInfo.address.state}, India. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${companyInfo.email}`}>{companyInfo.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Products and descriptions</h2>
      <p>
        Our pieces are made by hand. Hammered, cast and antiqued finishes vary slightly from piece to
        piece, and that variation is a property of the process rather than a defect. Photographs show
        a representative piece; colour on a screen is not a colour match. If an exact match matters,
        ask us for a physical sample before ordering.
      </p>
      <p>
        Dimensions and weights are nominal and subject to normal manufacturing tolerance.
      </p>

      <h2>Prices and payment</h2>
      <p>
        Retail prices are in Indian rupees and, where stated, include GST. We may change prices at any
        time, but never after you have paid for an order. Payment is processed by our payment provider
        over an encrypted connection; we do not receive or store your card details.
      </p>
      <p>
        If a price is displayed in error we will tell you before dispatch and you may cancel for a
        full refund.
      </p>

      <h2>Orders</h2>
      <p>
        Your order is an offer to buy. A contract is formed when we confirm dispatch. We may decline
        an order — for example where a piece is unavailable or a delivery address is outside the area
        we can serve — and will refund anything paid.
      </p>

      <h2>Trade and export orders</h2>
      <p>
        Wholesale, export and bespoke orders are not governed by this page. They are governed by the
        proforma invoice and the specification agreed for that order, which take precedence over
        anything stated here.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The content of this site — photographs, text, designs and product drawings — belongs to
        {companyInfo.name}. Where we manufacture to a customer's drawing, that drawing and any tooling
        made from it remain the customer's, and we do not offer that design to another buyer.
      </p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        We stand behind our manufacturing. Nothing here limits liability for death, personal injury or
        fraud, or any liability that cannot be limited under Indian law. Beyond that, our liability
        for any order is limited to the value of that order. We are not liable for indirect or
        consequential loss such as lost profit or lost business.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of India. The courts at Moradabad, Uttar Pradesh have
        jurisdiction.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. The version in force is the one published here on the day you place
        your order.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
